# Duration-Aware-MDP

## Overview
This repository contains the codebase and experimental results for the thesis: Towards Healthy User Engagement: Episode Length Control in Finite-Horizon Absorbing MDPs. 

The work implements a Reinforcement Learning (RL) framework modeling Markov Decision Processes (MDPs) with absorbing states. It specifically focuses on optimizing interaction duration and managing stochastic exit probabilities in both single-user and contextual multi-user settings.

## Repository Structure

The project is divided into two main directories:

### 1. `code/`
Contains all algorithmic implementations, environment models and execution scripts for the switch-aware exploration strategies. 

### 2. `results/`
Stores all experimental results, including the cumulative regret curves and the absorption step plots for each configuration tested.
